1	# Frontend Assessment API Contract
2	
3	This contract is fixed for the assessment. Implement it with `msw@2.14.6` handlers as described in `MOCKING_GUIDE.md`. No backend or direct fixture transport is permitted.
4	
5	Base path: `/api`
6	
7	All timestamps crossing the client boundary are ISO 8601 UTC strings. The UI displays them in the user's local timezone.
8	
9	## Data Types
10	
11	```ts
12	type SessionType = "training" | "camp" | "private";
13	type SessionStatus = "scheduled" | "full" | "cancelled" | "completed";
14	type Visibility = "public" | "invite-only";
15	
16	interface CoachSummary {
17	  id: string;
18	  name: string;
19	  email: string;
20	}
21	
22	interface LocationSummary {
23	  name: string;
24	  address: string;
25	}
26	
27	interface SessionSummary {
28	  id: string;
29	  title: string;
30	  type: SessionType;
31	  status: SessionStatus;
32	  startsAt: string;
33	  durationMinutes: number;
34	  capacity: number;
35	  bookedCount: number;
36	  visibility: Visibility;
37	  coach: CoachSummary;
38	  location: LocationSummary;
39	  updatedAt: string;
40	}
41	
42	interface SessionDetails extends SessionSummary {
43	  description: string | null;
44	  trainerNotes: string | null;
45	  createdAt: string;
46	  cancellation: null | {
47	    reason: string | null;
48	    cancelledAt: string;
49	  };
50	}
51	
52	interface ApiError {
53	  error: {
54	    code: string;
55	    message: string;
56	    fieldErrors?: Record<string, string>;
57	  };
58	}
59	```
60	
61	## GET /api/sessions
62	
63	Required query parameters:
64	
65	| Name | Type | Default | Notes |
66	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
67	| `query` | string | empty | Searches title, coach name, and location. |
68	| `status` | SessionStatus | empty | One status in v1. |
69	
70	Filtering by `type` and implementing pagination are optional extensions. The required response retains `page: 1` and `pageSize: 10` metadata.
71	
72	Response `200`:
73	
74	```ts
75	interface SessionsResponse {
76	  data: SessionSummary[];
77	  meta: {
78	    page: number;
79	    pageSize: number;
80	    total: number;
81	  };
82	}
83	```
84	
85	Use `fixtures/sessions.json` as the default response. It contains five records, `page: 1`, `pageSize: 10`, and `total: 5`. MSW handlers must apply `query` and `status` before calculating `meta.total`.
86	
87	Errors:
88	
89	- `400 INVALID_FILTER`: malformed query parameter.
90	- `500 SESSIONS_UNAVAILABLE`: list cannot be loaded.
91	
92	## GET /api/sessions/:sessionId
93	
94	Response `200`: `SessionDetails`.
95	
96	Use the matching `fixtures/session-details/<sessionId>.json` file. Every session in the default list has a corresponding details fixture.
97	
98	Errors:
99	
100	- `404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND`: the URL refers to an unknown or deleted session.
101	- `500 SESSION_DETAILS_UNAVAILABLE`: details cannot be loaded.
102	
103	## GET /api/coaches
104	
105	Response `200`:
106	
107	```ts
108	interface CoachesResponse {
109	  data: CoachSummary[];
110	}
111	```
112	
113	Use `fixtures/coaches.json` as the default response.
114	
115	Errors:
