1	# Frontend Assessment API Contract
2	
3	This contract is fixed for the assessment. Implement it with `msw@2.14.6` handlers as described in `MOCKING_GUIDE.md`. No backend or direct fixture transport is permitted.
4	
5	Base path: `/api`
6	
7	All timestamps crossing the client boundary are ISO 8601 UTC strings. The UI displays them in the user's local timezone.
8	
9	## Data Types
10	
11	```ts
12	type SessionType = "training" | "camp" | "private";
13	type SessionStatus = "scheduled" | "full" | "cancelled" | "completed";
14	type Visibility = "public" | "invite-only";
15	
16	interface CoachSummary {
17	  id: string;
18	  name: string;
19	  email: string;
20	}
21	
22	interface LocationSummary {
23	  name: string;
24	  address: string;
25	}
26	
27	interface SessionSummary {
28	  id: string;
29	  title: string;
30	  type: SessionType;
31	  status: SessionStatus;
32	  startsAt: string;
33	  durationMinutes: number;
34	  capacity: number;
35	  bookedCount: number;
36	  visibility: Visibility;
37	  coach: CoachSummary;
38	  location: LocationSummary;
39	  updatedAt: string;
40	}
41	
42	interface SessionDetails extends SessionSummary {
43	  description: string | null;
44	  trainerNotes: string | null;
45	  createdAt: string;
46	  cancellation: null | {
47	    reason: string | null;
48	    cancelledAt: string;
49	  };
50	}
51	
52	interface ApiError {
53	  error: {
54	    code: string;
55	    message: string;
56	    fieldErrors?: Record<string, string>;
57	  };
58	}
59	```
60	
61	## GET /api/sessions
62	
63	Required query parameters:
64	
65	| Name | Type | Default | Notes |
66	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
67	| `query` | string | empty | Searches title, coach name, and location. |
68	| `status` | SessionStatus | empty | One status in v1. |
69	
70	Filtering by `type` and implementing pagination are optional extensions. The required response retains `page: 1` and `pageSize: 10` metadata.
71	
72	Response `200`:
73	
74	```ts
75	interface SessionsResponse {
76	  data: SessionSummary[];
77	  meta: {
78	    page: number;
79	    pageSize: number;
80	    total: number;
81	  };
82	}
83	```
84	
85	Use `fixtures/sessions.json` as the default response. It contains five records, `page: 1`, `pageSize: 10`, and `total: 5`. MSW handlers must apply `query` and `status` before calculating `meta.total`.
86	
87	Errors:
88	
89	- `400 INVALID_FILTER`: malformed query parameter.
90	- `500 SESSIONS_UNAVAILABLE`: list cannot be loaded.
91	
92	## GET /api/sessions/:sessionId
93	
94	Response `200`: `SessionDetails`.
95	
96	Use the matching `fixtures/session-details/<sessionId>.json` file. Every session in the default list has a corresponding details fixture.
97	
98	Errors:
99	
100	- `404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND`: the URL refers to an unknown or deleted session.
101	- `500 SESSION_DETAILS_UNAVAILABLE`: details cannot be loaded.
102	
103	## GET /api/coaches
104	
105	Response `200`:
106	
107	```ts
108	interface CoachesResponse {
109	  data: CoachSummary[];
110	}
111	```
112	
113	Use `fixtures/coaches.json` as the default response.
114	
115	Errors:
116	
117	- `500 COACHES_UNAVAILABLE`: coach choices cannot be loaded. The create form must not pretend it can submit a valid coach selection.
118	
119	## POST /api/sessions
120	
121	Request:
122	
123	```ts
124	interface CreateSessionRequest {
125	  title: string;
126	  type: SessionType;
127	  startsAt: string;
128	  durationMinutes: number;
129	  coachId: string;
130	  locationName: string;
131	  locationAddress: string;
132	  capacity: number;
133	  visibility: Visibility;
134	  description?: string | null;
135	  trainerNotes?: string | null;
136	}
137	```
138	
139	Both `locationName` and `locationAddress` are required by the product specification and this contract.
140	
141	Response `201`: `SessionDetails` with generated identifiers and timestamps. The successful mock response must echo the normalized submitted values, use the selected coach from the coaches fixture, and become available through both list and details reads.
142	
143	Required errors:
144	
145	- `400 VALIDATION_FAILED`: includes `fieldErrors` where available.
146	- `500 CREATE_SESSION_FAILED`: unexpected failure.
147	
148	Optional error: `409 COACH_SCHEDULE_CONFLICT` when another session overlaps for the selected coach.
149	
150	The client must prevent accidental duplicate submissions but must not manufacture idempotency guarantees that the contract does not provide.
151	
152	## Optional: POST /api/sessions/:sessionId/cancel
153	
154	Request:
155	
156	```ts
157	interface CancelSessionRequest {
158	  reason?: string | null;
159	}
160	```
161	
162	Response `200`: updated `SessionDetails` with `status: "cancelled"` and a populated `cancellation` object. The corresponding list summary must also expose the new status.
163	
164	Errors:
165	
166	- `403 SESSION_CANCEL_FORBIDDEN`: current user has read-only access.
167	- `404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND`: session no longer exists.
168	- `409 SESSION_STATE_CHANGED`: session was already cancelled or completed; refresh details from the server.
169	- `500 CANCEL_SESSION_FAILED`: unexpected failure.
170	
171	## Optional Permission Input
172	
173	Authentication is out of scope. An implementation that includes optional cancellation or read-only behavior may provide one current permission:
174	
175	```ts
176	type SessionPermission = "manage" | "read-only";
177	```
178	
179	`manage` exposes create and eligible cancellation actions. `read-only` does not render enabled mutation controls. Client-side hiding is a UX behavior, not a claim of backend authorization.
180	
181	Permission injection belongs at the mock/application boundary. It is not a new backend endpoint.
182	
183	## Deterministic Mock Scenarios
184	
185	The required scenarios are `normal`, `empty`, `list-error`, `details-error`, `coaches-error`, and `create-error`.
186	
187	The supplied `create-conflict`, `cancel-forbidden`, `cancel-conflict`, `read-only`, `slow-refresh`, and `unknown-session` scenarios are optional extensions.
188	
189	The candidate chooses how to select scenarios. Scenario selection is assessment infrastructure, not part of the external API contract. Presentation components consume ordinary success or error results and must not branch on scenario names. See `MOCKING_GUIDE.md` for the complete mock boundary requirements.
190	
191	## Fixture Clock
192	
193	`fixtures/fixture-clock.json` contains the reference instant used by all supplied timestamps. At mock startup:
194	
195	1. read `referenceNow`;
196	2. compute the difference between the actual current instant and the reference instant;
197	3. shift every fixture `startsAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `cancelledAt` value by that difference;
198	4. expose the shifted value as a normal ISO 8601 UTC string.
199	
200	This transformation occurs only in the MSW boundary. Production-facing types and presentation components remain unaware of it. Tests should freeze time and use the same transformation.
201	
202	## Contract Authority
203	
204	The candidate may add local view models and normalization functions. Changing endpoint paths, required request fields, response fields, or error codes requires an explicit proposal in task documentation and evaluator approval. Do not silently adapt the contract to simplify implementation.
